AI Web Annotator


	Description

Chrome Extension (Manifest V3) to interactively annotate any web page
and export structured DOM context, screenshots, and prompts for AI.


	Requirements

This project requires Node.js 20 or later, npm, and Google Chrome (or
any Chromium-based web browser). Docker is optional for containerized
development.


	Installation

Install dependencies and build the extension:

    npm install
    npm run build

Load the extension into Google Chrome:

1. Open Google Chrome and navigate to chrome://extensions/
2. Enable "Developer mode" in the top-right corner.
3. Click "Load unpacked" and select the dist/ directory.


	Usage

1. Click the extension icon on any page to freeze interactions.
2. Click elements to place numbered badges and enter comments.
3. Click "Terminer & Exporter" in the HUD:
   - Downloads a screenshot (.png) with numbered badges.
   - Downloads structured DOM context (.json) with selectors and XPath.
   - Copies a formatted AI prompt to clipboard.


	Testing

Run the automated test suite with the following command:

    npm test

All tests should pass before changes are submitted.


	Development

To run the development build with automatic file watching:

    npm run dev

To create a distributable zip archive:

    npm run package

Or run the watch mode inside Docker:

    docker compose up


